<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for April 12.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for April 12.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, has announced the following forecasts and data for gas consumption in the period April 10 to 12.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 10 (actual) 191 mcm, 45 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 11 (forecast) 204 mcm, 48 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 12 (forecast) 204 mcm, 48 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>Apr 10 (actual) 11.6 Celsius, SNT 9.0 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 11 (forecast) 7.9 Celsius, SNT 9.1 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 12 (forecast) 7.9 Celsius, SNT 9.2 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption on Friday, with none expected on Saturday</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
